agent: Free the cached PIN's buffer after each use

Each signature with a PIN-protected key reads the PIN cached in the kernel's
keyring into a fresh buffer that memcall maps and locks, and the callback
returns that buffer without ever freeing it. Every signature leaks its
locked pages, so once the unit's locked-memory limit fills, every later
signature fails with "<memcall> could not acquire lock ... limit reached"
until the agent restarts. On a busy machine that took three hours.

Copy the PIN out and free the buffer at once, as the askpass path already
hands back a plain slice. Upstream's fix (pull request 135) instead hands
the buffer to the caller to free after signing; this is the smaller change
for 0.9.0.

diff -ru a/cmd/ssh-tpm-agent/main.go b/cmd/ssh-tpm-agent/main.go
--- a/cmd/ssh-tpm-agent/main.go
+++ b/cmd/ssh-tpm-agent/main.go
@@ -274,7 +274,11 @@
 			case err == nil:
 				slog.Debug("providing cached userauth for key", slog.String("fp", key.Fingerprint()))
 				// TODO: This is not great, but easier for now
-				return auth.Read(), nil
+				pin := slices.Clone(auth.Read())
+				if err := auth.Free(); err != nil {
+					slog.Warn("freeing the cached userauth's buffer", slog.Any("err", err))
+				}
+				return pin, nil
 			}
 			return nil, fmt.Errorf("failed getting pin for key: %w", err)
 		},
